  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">- A dashboard for monitoring selected resilience indicators is developed
- A regional disaster preparedness and response plan is in place
- Capacities on systematic data collection during crises are developed
- A post-drought recovery strategy is developed</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="FR">1.	90% of the food consumed by Djiboutians is imported, which makes Djibouti specially affected by the global increase on energy and food prices in the past few months.
2.	85% of the GDP of Djibouti comes from the seaport activity, and 90% of that activity is imports and exports from Ethiopia. The COVID-19 crisis exacerbated the fragility of this mono-specialized business model, which leaves 80% of youth out of job.
3.	Conflict in Ethiopia has aggravated the isolation of Djibouti, surrounded by Somalia, Yemen and Eritrea, and reduced State income by at least 20%.
4.	The country is facing the third consecutive below average rainy season, as the rest of the Horn of Africa. The ongoing drought has exacerbated existing vulnerabilities of the population, that is already affected by multiple shocks, affecting the purchasing power of the population and especially food security.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="FR">- Faire une &#xe9;valuation de limpact de la s&#xe8;cheresse &#xe0; Djibouti 
- Sur la base des r&#xe9;sultats de l&#xe9;tude, pr&#xe9;parer une strat&#xe9;gie de redressement post s&#xe8;cheresse
- Appuyer le minist&#xe8;re du commerce &#xe0; lutter contre les inflations opportuniste et &#xe0; am&#xe9;liorer la collecte des donn&#xe9;es
- Renforcer les bureaux d&#xe9;centralis&#xe9;es en charge de la gestion des risques et de catastrophe</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
